<title>FRANCE: EU sells German intervention barley, rye - trade.</title>
<headline>EU sells German intervention barley, rye - trade.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday sold around 9,000 tonnes of German intervention barley at a minimum price of 101.50 Ecus per tonne for export to countries outside the EU, grain traders said.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committee in Brussels also sold 21,180 tonnes of German intervention rye at a minimum price of 100.13 Ecus per tonne, they said.</p>
</text>
